--- Input-side provenance narrowing at a marked crossing (DR-0027 I-IFC3
--- refinement). A marked egress -- one whose payload is carried ENTIRELY by a
--- `coerce ... declassified|endorsed` output -- previously inherited the whole
--- rule read set: every confidential source in the rule needed a grant for the
--- crossing to arm, even sources that never fed the coercion. The narrowing
--- computes the CARRIED source set from the coercion's ARGUMENT roots: a root
--- attributed to source S contributes S; an unattributable root (agent turn
--- output, exec result, unrecognized binding) widens the carried set to ALL
--- rule sources -- the fail-closed fallback, identical to the pre-narrowing
--- behavior. The model is axis-neutral: `leak` stands for either the denied
--- confidentiality flow, declassify grants, or the denied integrity influence,
--- endorse grants; both narrow by the same carried-set rule.
---
--- Soundness shape (the field-signature discipline): the carried set never
--- UNDER-reports. A root attributed to S contributes exactly S; an unknown
--- root contributes EVERYTHING; so a source truly feeding the coercion is
--- always carried (coverage), while a source with no path into the arguments
--- is dropped only when every root is attributed (bite, the real refinement).
--- Chaining through an intermediate unmarked coercion is an attribution detail
--- -- its output root expands to ITS argument roots, a total mixing point --
--- exercised by the Rust end-to-end tests; here a chained root is simply the
--- union it resolves to.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-INFOFLOW-INPUT-PROVENANCE is
  protecting BOOL .

  sorts Src Level Root RootList Cfg .
  subsort Root < RootList .

  ops sA sB : -> Src [ctor] .

  --- two-point confidentiality lattice: hi needs a grant to cross, lo never leaks.
  ops lo hi : -> Level [ctor] .

  --- an argument root attributed to a source, or an unattributable root.
  op rs : Src -> Root [ctor] .
  op unknown : -> Root [ctor] .
  op nilR : -> RootList [ctor] .
  op _._ : Root RootList -> RootList [ctor] .

  op none : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op __ : Cfg Cfg -> Cfg [ctor assoc comm id: none] .

  --- ground-truth inputs supplied per scenario. Grantedness lives INSIDE the
  --- src constructor -- src(S, level, granted?) -- so the deny rule's condition
  --- needs no whole-configuration lookup: an AC-extension sub-match (a rule
  --- matching only part of the soup) then evaluates the identical condition,
  --- which is what makes the negative searches trustworthy.
  op src : Src Level Bool -> Cfg [ctor] . --- source, confidentiality, grant covering the sink
  op crossing : RootList -> Cfg [ctor] .  --- the marked egress, its coercion's argument roots
  op leak : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  eq leak leak = leak .

  var S : Src .  var L : Level .  var R : Root .  var RL : RootList .  var C : Cfg .

  op mentions : RootList Src -> Bool .
  eq mentions(nilR, S) = false .
  eq mentions((rs(S) . RL), S) = true .
  eq mentions((R . RL), S) = mentions(RL, S) [owise] .

  op hasUnknown : RootList -> Bool .
  eq hasUnknown(nilR) = false .
  eq hasUnknown((unknown . RL)) = true .
  eq hasUnknown((R . RL)) = hasUnknown(RL) [owise] .

  --- S is carried by the crossing iff a root is attributed to S, OR any root is
  --- unattributable (the fallback widens to every source -- fail-closed).
  op carried : RootList Src -> Bool .
  eq carried(RL, S) = hasUnknown(RL) or mentions(RL, S) .

  --- The narrowed denial: a confidential source CARRIED by the marked crossing
  --- and not covered by a grant denies the flow. A source NOT carried is not
  --- checked against this sink at all -- the narrowing. lo sources never leak;
  --- a granted source arms instead of leaking.
  crl [deny] : crossing(RL) src(S, hi, false) C => crossing(RL) src(S, hi, false) C leak
    if carried(RL, S) = true .
endm
